#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:1
msgid "Adding Language Support via the Plugin Path"
msgstr "Adding Language Support via the Plugin Path"

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:3
msgid "This guide walks through adding full AST-aware language support to lang-check. It uses **TinyLang** (the project's reference demo language) as a running example."
msgstr "This guide walks through adding full AST-aware language support to lang-check. It uses **TinyLang** (the project's reference demo language) as a running example."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:6
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Overview"

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:8
msgid "The plugin path gives a language first-class integration with lang-check:"
msgstr "The plugin path gives a language first-class integration with lang-check:"

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:10
msgid "**AST-aware prose extraction** -- tree-sitter parses the document, and a Rust module walks the syntax tree to collect only the nodes that contain human-written prose."
msgstr "**AST-aware prose extraction** -- tree-sitter parses the document, and a Rust module walks the syntax tree to collect only the nodes that contain human-written prose."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:13
msgid "**Math exclusion zones** -- inline and display math are recognized by the grammar and either skipped entirely or replaced with spaces (preserving byte offsets so diagnostics map back correctly)."
msgstr "**Math exclusion zones** -- inline and display math are recognized by the grammar and either skipped entirely or replaced with spaces (preserving byte offsets so diagnostics map back correctly)."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:16
msgid "**One description of the markup between words** -- what may appear in the gap between two prose words is written once, as a `gap::Syntax` function, and both the \"do these words join up\" test and the exclusion zones are derived from it."
msgstr "**One description of the markup between words** -- what may appear in the gap between two prose words is written once, as a `gap::Syntax` function, and both the \"do these words join up\" test and the exclusion zones are derived from it."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:19
msgid "**Code block / comment skipping** -- fenced code, inline code, and comments are pruned from the AST walk so they never reach the grammar checker."
msgstr "**Code block / comment skipping** -- fenced code, inline code, and comments are pruned from the AST walk so they never reach the grammar checker."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:21
msgid "**Structural command filtering** -- commands whose arguments are identifiers or metadata (e.g. `@import`, `@ref`) are distinguished from commands whose arguments are prose (e.g. `@title`, `@note`)."
msgstr "**Structural command filtering** -- commands whose arguments are identifiers or metadata (e.g. `@import`, `@ref`) are distinguished from commands whose arguments are prose (e.g. `@title`, `@note`)."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:25
msgid "The end result is that lang-check only grammar-checks real prose, with accurate source positions for every diagnostic."
msgstr "The end result is that lang-check only grammar-checks real prose, with accurate source positions for every diagnostic."

