#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:350
msgid "**3. Gap syntax** -- the one function a new language has to write."
msgstr "**3. Gap syntax** -- the one function a new language has to write."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:352
msgid "A gap is the source between two prose words, and it decides two things: whether those words belong to the same prose block, and which byte ranges the checker must not see. Both come from the same question -- *what token starts here?* -- so the language answers it once, as a `gap::Syntax` function, and `gap::strip` and `gap::exclusions` derive the rest:"
msgstr "A gap is the source between two prose words, and it decides two things: whether those words belong to the same prose block, and which byte ranges the checker must not see. Both come from the same question -- *what token starts here?* -- so the language answers it once, as a `gap::Syntax` function, and `gap::strip` and `gap::exclusions` derive the rest:"

