msgstr "Points worth copying:"

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:394
msgid "**Return `None` for ordinary text.** Anything the function does not recognize is prose, and the scan advances one character."
msgstr "**Return `None` for ordinary text.** Anything the function does not recognize is prose, and the scan advances one character."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:396
msgid "**Match on `b[i..]`, not on indices.** The slice pattern carries the bounds check, so there is no `i + 1 < len` to forget. `[b'/', b'/', ..]` needs two bytes present; a lone trailing `/` falls through to `_` on its own."
msgstr "**Match on `b[i..]`, not on indices.** The slice pattern carries the bounds check, so there is no `i + 1 < len` to forget. `[b'/', b'/', ..]` needs two bytes present; a lone trailing `/` falls through to `_` on its own."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:399
msgid "**Order the arms longest-prefix first.** `$$` before `$`, `//` before a bare marker. The first matching arm wins."
msgstr "**Order the arms longest-prefix first.** `$$` before `$`, `//` before a bare marker. The first matching arm wins."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:401
msgid "**`end` must be greater than `i`,** or the scan cannot make progress."
msgstr "**`end` must be greater than `i`,** or the scan cannot make progress."

#: ../../guide-plugin-language.md:402
msgid "**Work on bytes.** Every delimiter above is single-byte ASCII, so a byte offset that matches is always a character boundary, and non-ASCII prose passes through untouched."
msgstr "**Work on bytes.** Every delimiter above is single-byte ASCII, so a byte offset that matches is always a character boundary, and non-ASCII prose passes through untouched."

